# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Every Dockerfile in infra/docker/ builds from the repository root, because a
# pnpm workspace needs its lockfile and every member manifest to resolve. That
# makes this file load-bearing in two ways: it keeps the context small enough
# that a build is fast, and it keeps things out of images that must never be in
# one.
#
# The second is the important one. A .env file copied into a layer is still in
# that layer after it is deleted in a later step, and an image is a file that
# gets pushed to a registry.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and local configuration --------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
infra/seaweedfs/s3_config.json

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is excluded deliberately, not as an oversight. The image
# installs from the lockfile inside the build, for the target platform. A
# host's node_modules carries the host's architecture and its own binaries;
# copying it in is how a build passes on a developer's laptop and fails on the
# node.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
dist
build
out
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Test and coverage -----------------------------------------------------
coverage
**/coverage
.nyc_output
playwright-report
test-results
**/__snapshots__

# --- Editor and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Documentation and project tracking ------------------------------------
# Not needed to build a runnable image, and they change on nearly every commit,
# which would invalidate the build cache for no reason.
docs
project
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# --- Infrastructure --------------------------------------------------------
# Config that is mounted at runtime, never baked in. Mounting means a config
# change is a restart rather than a rebuild and a registry push.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
infra/caddy
infra/otel
infra/prometheus
infra/grafana
infra/postgres
infra/seaweedfs

# infra/docker and infra/piston are NOT excluded:
#   infra/docker  — the Dockerfiles themselves must be in the context
#   infra/piston  — packages.json and install-runtimes.sh are baked into the
#                   Piston image at build time, because an exec node has no
#                   egress and cannot fetch a runtime at boot

# --- Local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
tmp
.tmp
*.log
.cache
.claude
